{"id": "73086ceacffb1f5c5722", "repository": "danoszz/penthera", "commit_sha": "9b12fb9777ef67d4a50083bf8de2f0d565368661", "skill_path": "plugin/skills/penthera/SKILL.md", "source_url": "https://github.com/danoszz/penthera/blob/9b12fb9777ef67d4a50083bf8de2f0d565368661/plugin/skills/penthera/SKILL.md", "git_blob_sha": "84ac48961f1bf1ff36de2ac7fbeb5e036e886348", "sha256": "6eae3e13441895c53209c2e665840da180859283c3ff0bd515ea651ebf3a5e9a", "bytes": 30356, "collected_at": "2026-11-06T11:25:08.804200+00:00", "state": "collected", "raw_path": "raw/danoszz/penthera/9b12fb9777ef67d4a50083bf8de2f0d565368661/plugin/skills/penthera/SKILL.md", "execution_status": "not_executed", "quality_status": "not_evaluated", "license_candidates": ["LICENSE", "plugin/LICENSE"], "repository_manifest": "manifests/danoszz/penthera/9b12fb9777ef67d4a50083bf8de2f0d565368661.json", "local_package_files": ["plugin/skills/penthera/SKILL.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/references/authorization.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/references/output-and-ci.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/references/profiles-and-flags.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/references/remediation.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/references/reporting.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/references/secure-defaults.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/references/troubleshooting.md", "plugin/skills/penthera/scripts/preflight.sh", "plugin/skills/penthera/scripts/validate-report.mjs", "plugin/skills/penthera/scripts/validate-report.sh"], "local_package_files_not_exported": [], "external_dependency_status": "not_fetched_or_verified", "path_review_hints": [], "frontmatter_raw": "name: penthera\ndescription: >\n  Offline cyber security agent for the user's own apps and AI coding tools, run\n  locally with the Penthera CLI; open R&D, measured in public. Sets it up in one\n  command (\"set up penthera in this repo\"). Scans the user's own live URL and repo\n  (TLS, headers, auth, OpenAPI, secrets incl. AI keys, opt-in injection); checks npm\n  and Python dependencies offline (\"is this dependency safe?\", \"what changed in my\n  deps?\", \"install X safely\", \"any AGPL in our deps?\"); blocks secrets and risky\n  agent config before commit (\"add a pre-commit hook\"); audits AI tooling (\"audit\n  my MCP servers / skills / hooks\", \"check this skill before I install it\"); fixes\n  findings on a local branch and re-scans to verify (\"scan and fix my app\"); writes\n  reports and evidence (\"report for my auditor / manager\", NIS2, SARIF, baseline\n  diff). Use when the user asks to scan, audit, harden, fix, or review the security\n  of their own app, staging URL, localhost, repo, dependencies, or agent setup. Do\n  NOT use for targets without explicit authorization.\nlicense: MIT\ncompatibility: Node.js 22+, the Penthera CLI (npx -y penthera@2.3.2, npm install -g, or node bin/penthera.js from a checkout), network access to the target for URL scans. macOS only for --machine.\nallowed-tools: \"Read\"\nmetadata:\n  author: danoszz\n  version: 2.3.2\n  category: security", "declared_name": "penthera", "format_status": "header_present_not_schema_validated"}
